{"id": "t0055", "rev": 2, "kind": "text", "answers": "0001", "t": 1789604780.957583, "iso": "2026-09-16 19:26:20", "from": "student", "text": "You plug in gamma, you clearly get zero. And composition of nonzero polynomials is non-zero - we\u2019re in an integral domain.", "signal": null, "read": false}
{"id": "t0055", "rev": 3, "kind": "text", "answers": "0001", "t": 1789605073.647319, "iso": "2026-09-16 19:31:13", "from": "student", "text": "f is non-constant. It can\u2019t be constant because it evaluates to zero at an input and yet is the nonzero polynomial", "signal": null, "read": false}
